Fetch wraps the yt-dlp command-line tool at runtime. yt-dlp is not bundled
with Fetch and is licensed separately under the Unlicense. See:
https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/blob/master/LICENSE

Fetch wraps the ffmpeg command-line tool at runtime. ffmpeg is not bundled
with Fetch and is licensed separately under LGPL v2.1 (with GPL v2 options
for some components). See:
https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

Neither yt-dlp nor ffmpeg are linked into the Fetch binary. They are
invoked as subprocesses via the macOS Process API, with the user
installing them independently via Homebrew or similar.
